      "id": "claim_8f80b7f2c8804b0da48966618477b60b",
      "statement": "Distributed-systems design places responsibility for metadata, ordering, retries, and repair across control and data paths; GFS separates master metadata from direct client-to-chunkserver transfer, Bigtable uses GFS and Chubby as substrate and coordinator, and MapReduce owns scheduling and worker recovery.",
